When a provider or insurer rejects an initial No Surprises Act (NSA) dispute, standard correspondence rarely resolves the issue. Rejections typically stem from template-driven billing systems ignoring statutory citations or insurers attempting to classify OON services as non-covered under network exceptions.
To overcome a rejection, the dispute must shift from a voluntary request for bill correction to a formal administrative demand with agency notification under federal (45 C.F.R. Part 149) and state (PA Act 146 of 2022 / FCEUA) enforcement protocols.
